    {
      "short_id": "short269",
      "angle": "The Supreme Court vacated and remanded without holding any arbitration clause valid or ordering anyone to arbitrate.",
      "avoids": "No claim that the clauses were held valid; no merged families; no named Supreme Court author or guessed vote; no invented relationship.",
      "funnel_question_left_for_longform": "What happened to Brown, Taylor, and Marchio after remand, and why were their outcomes different?",
      "loop": true,
      "loop_join": "The final line returns to the word vacated and what it did not decide.",
      "era": "West Virginia, 2009-2012",
      "lines": [
        {
          "id": "L1",
          "text": "The Supreme Court did not hold these nursing-home arbitration clauses valid. It vacated the state judgment and sent the cases back.",
          "delivery": "intense",
          "source_lines": [
            "The decision of the State Supreme Court of Appeals must be vacated."
          ],
          "claims": []
        },
        {
          "id": "L2",
          "text": "It did not order anyone to arbitrate, decide whether the families could sue, or settle what the signed papers ultimately meant.",
          "delivery": "building",
          "source_lines": [
            "It did not order anyone to arbitrate anything."
          ],
          "claims": []
        },
        {
          "id": "L3",
          "text": "For Brown and Taylor, the state court had to reconsider unconscionability under ordinary contract principles not aimed specifically at arbitration.",
          "delivery": "building",
          "source_lines": [
            "So, the instruction."
          ],
          "claims": []
        },
        {
          "id": "L4",
          "text": "For Marchio, the earlier state opinion had never reached any non-public-policy reason that her different agreement might be unenforceable.",
          "delivery": "building",
          "source_lines": [
            "Marchio's paper was not that paper."
          ],
          "claims": []
        },
        {
          "id": "L5",
          "text": "The federal disposition was vacated and remanded. That describes Washington's judgment, not a final ruling that the clauses were enforceable.",
          "delivery": "building",
          "source_lines": [
            "The petition for certiorari is granted."
          ],
          "claims": []
        },
        {
          "id": "L6",
          "text": "On remand, West Virginia overruled one syllabus point exactly as instructed, then retained the rest of its contract-law analysis.",
          "delivery": "building",
          "source_lines": [
            "In accordance with the Supreme Court's mandate, we overrule Syllabus Point 21 of Brown One."
          ],
          "claims": []
        },
        {
          "id": "L7",
          "text": "Its final outcomes were not uniform: Brown and Taylor were reversed and remanded; Marchio's certified question was answered.",
          "delivery": "building",
          "source_lines": [
            "Then the disposition, and it is not one thing."
          ],
          "claims": []
        },
        {
          "id": "L8",
          "text": "So remember what vacated meant here: the Supreme Court removed the judgment and required another analysis; it never validated the clauses.",
          "delivery": "calm",
          "source_lines": [
            "The Supreme Court of the United States did not hold that any of these three arbitration clauses was valid."
          ],
          "claims": []
        }
      ],
