    {
      "short_id": "short270",
      "angle": "West Virginia used unusually sharp language against Supreme Court FAA doctrine, then complied on one point while preserving contract-law analysis.",
      "avoids": "No claim that the clauses were held valid; no merged families; no named Supreme Court author or guessed vote; no invented relationship.",
      "funnel_question_left_for_longform": "Who controls when a state court and the Supreme Court disagree about federal arbitration law and state contract law?",
      "loop": true,
      "loop_join": "The last line returns to the two quoted words that opened the conflict.",
      "era": "West Virginia, 2009-2012",
      "lines": [
        {
          "id": "L1",
          "text": "West Virginia's highest court called the Supreme Court's arbitration reasoning tendentious and created from whole cloth. Those were the state court's words.",
          "delivery": "intense",
          "source_lines": [
            "It called this Court's interpretation of the Federal Arbitration Act tendentious. It called it created from whole cloth."
          ],
          "claims": []
        },
        {
          "id": "L2",
          "text": "The Supreme Court answered that the state's interpretation was incorrect and inconsistent with clear instructions in its own precedents.",
          "delivery": "building",
          "source_lines": [
            "To the language about tendentious reasoning, one sentence."
          ],
          "claims": []
        },
        {
          "id": "L3",
          "text": "It added a constitutional command: once the Court interprets federal law, a state court may not contradict or refuse to implement that rule.",
          "delivery": "building",
          "source_lines": [
            "The citation is the Supremacy Clause."
          ],
          "claims": []
        },
        {
          "id": "L4",
          "text": "The decision was per curiam: no Justice was named as author, and the opinion reported no vote.",
          "delivery": "building",
          "source_lines": [
            "It is five pages long, and it is per curiam — an opinion issued by the Court with no author's name on it and no vote reported."
          ],
          "claims": []
        },
        {
          "id": "L5",
          "text": "Washington vacated the judgment and remanded. It did not itself decide whether any particular arbitration clause was valid.",
          "delivery": "building",
          "source_lines": [
            "The decision of the State Supreme Court of Appeals must be vacated."
          ],
          "claims": []
        },
        {
          "id": "L6",
          "text": "Back in West Virginia, the court obeyed by overruling the one syllabus point the Supreme Court had rejected.",
          "delivery": "building",
          "source_lines": [
            "Overrule. Not vacate, not modify, not distinguish."
          ],
          "claims": []
        },
        {
          "id": "L7",
          "text": "It then said the mandate did not require changing its remaining analysis of ordinary state contract law, including unconscionability.",
          "delivery": "building",
          "source_lines": [
            "We otherwise find that the Supreme Court's decision does not counsel us to alter our original analysis of West Virginia's common law of contracts."
          ],
          "claims": []
        },
        {
          "id": "L8",
          "text": "So the state court complied on the federal rule but preserved the rest, leaving the conflict framed by its opening words: tendentious, whole cloth.",
          "delivery": "calm",
          "source_lines": [
            "And the court did not take back the language that had got it reversed."
          ],
          "claims": []
        }
      ],
